{{text}}

Answer them, and answer them by **sending a Message**: `POST /messages` on the Gateway's
Agent server, with a body of `{"userId": "{{userId}}", "text": "your answer"}`. Your system
prompt says where that server is and what else is on it.

That call is the only thing in this deployment that reaches a person. Your final reply here
is read by nobody: the Run records that it finished and not what you said, so an answer you
write only into this conversation, or into a file in the Workspace, arrives nowhere.

One call is one person. This message is {{userId}}'s and your answer goes to {{userId}} and
to no one else.

Most of what {{userId}} has said to you before is in this conversation already, because all
of their messages arrive in one Session. A Session is a lossy record and drops what it can no
longer hold, so `GET /messages?user={{userId}}` is where their Messages durably are: a page
at a time, both directions, oldest first within the page. `GET /signals?limit=` is what has
arrived recently from anybody.

Keep it to a couple of sentences.
